&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the UK’s market leading Financial Advisory Restructuring Tax team and make a real difference on a range of high profile and dynamic transactions. Our Financial Advisory Restructuring Tax team specialises in providing tax advice on the restructuring of financially distressed businesses. They have built a fantastic track record in recent years, leading on some of Europe’s largest and most complex restructuring processes. These include debt restructuring transactions, debt-for-equity swaps, business reconstructions via Restructuring Plans, Schemes of Arrangement and CVAs, and insolvency appointments. The variety of work really stands out, as does the friendly and supportive nature of the team. The team has a great mix of UK and international transactions work and is looking to recruit a corporation tax specialist at Associate Director level to build on the existing business capability and target a number of exciting developments in the restructuring market. This role is primarily advisory focused but will have some compliance responsibility. This is a unique opportunity to get involved. The role is technically interesting and personally rewarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your key areas of focus will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working directly with our financial advisory colleagues and external stakeholders including lenders, borrowers and legal advisors to understand the often complex commercial and legal requirements of each restructuring transaction;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing a strategy for achieving the commercial aims in a tax efficient manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing and preparing reports setting out the steps necessary to meet the aims of the transaction;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising insolvency practitioners involved in the restructuring on the tax consequences of their intended actions;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advising on the submission of appropriate tax returns or other documentation to tax authorities and liaising with them, as required;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting the business development activities of the team (you will have a broad scope to build relationships both internally and with key clients); and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contributing to the technical and personal development training of the broader team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To qualify for the role you must have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ACA/CTA or equivalent qualification or experience;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong UK tax technical skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, team playing and project management skills; &amp;nbsp;and&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to perform strongly under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Prior experience of transactions or insolvency processes is preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What can we offer you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;New joiners are supported by a week-long induction programme, and continuous improvement is achieved through a structured and tailored programme that suits your career development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As well as this we offer a whole host of benefits and reward including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 days holiday&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretionary Bonus Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cash benefits allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive investment in personal development &amp;amp; learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity and paternity leave (depending on length of service) and shared parental leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Group Income protection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Life assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to work schemes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular social, cultural and charitable activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Teneo&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Teneo is the global CEO advisory firm. We partner with our clients globally to do great things for a better future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drawing upon our global team and expansive network of senior advisors, we provide advisory services across our five business segments on a stand-alone or fully integrated basis to help our clients solve complex business challenges. Our clients include a significant number of the Fortune 100 and FTSE 100, as well as other corporations, financial institutions, and organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our full range of advisory services includes strategic communications, investor relations, financial transactions and restructuring, management consulting, physical and cyber risk, organizational design, board and executive search, geopolitics and government affairs, corporate governance, ESG and DE&amp;amp;I.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm has more than 1,800 employees located in 40+ offices around the world.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Backend Engineer on Development Health, you&#39;ll help make the systems that engineering teams rely on more reliable, maintainable, and easier to extend. You&#39;ll build and improve the automation, tooling, and data that help teams spot problems early and ship with less friction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As customer zero for GitLab, we support engineering workflows on GitLab&#39;s own product at scale. You&#39;ll use the product in demanding, real-world ways, surface the friction and gaps you find, and contribute to improvements that get built into the product for GitLab&#39;s customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll support work such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Health alerting and remediation routing for GitLab&#39;s core continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Flaky and slow test detection systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Engineering analytics and reporting that engineering teams use to make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Own and evolve core Development Health systems, from design through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Improve the reliability, maintainability, and test coverage of long-lived automation, and reduce reliance on undocumented knowledge by documenting and simplifying legacy systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Partner with engineering managers and product teams to identify workflow pain points and turn them into well-scoped, measurable improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Work with data to show whether changes improve engineering health, and use it to prioritize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Mentor intermediate engineers through code review, design feedback, and pairing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Communicate clearly in writing and asynchronously, including status, tradeoffs, and proposals for stakeholders across Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Monitor the health of production systems, troubleshoot incidents, and contribute to root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Use artificial intelligence (AI) agents and assistants to analyze issues and problem areas to help shape the team&#39;s product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Substantial experience as a backend or tooling engineer, with a track record of owning production systems end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Strong proficiency in Ruby, or the ability to become productive quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Experience maintaining or modernizing legacy codebases safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Comfort with CI/CD systems, application programming interfaces (APIs), and automation at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Independent problem-solving and clear, concise written communication: you spot problems early, raise risks proactively, and drive work to completion without close direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Experience writing automated unit and integration tests and taking part in collaborative code review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Experience using AI coding assistants to speed up development while critically reviewing their output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Optional experience: Rails; developer productivity, engineering analytics, or internal tooling; GitLab&#39;s product and open source contribution workflow; data pipelines or metrics reporting; or agent-based workflows that run in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Development Health is part of Developer Experience. Our work is mostly internal, and our customers are GitLab team members across an engineering organization of hundreds of engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re all-remote, asynchronous by default, and documentation-driven, in line with GitLab&#39;s values of collaboration, results, efficiency, diversity, inclusion and belonging, iteration, and transparency.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Engineering at GitLab believes that healthy teams deliver a healthy customer experience, and that command during a crisis shouldn&#39;t fall to whoever happens to be senior and available. GitLab&#39;s global Incident &amp;amp; Escalation Management (IM/EM) function coordinates critical incidents, complex multi-team engagements, and executive-level escalations for enterprise customers. As Escalation Manager, you&#39;ll own complex, executive, and commercial escalations where customer trust and the relationship are at stake, alongside or independently of a technical issue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this functional role, you&#39;ll advocate for customers inside GitLab, coordinate teams toward resolution, and lead relationship repair after the event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own complex, executive, and commercial escalations end-to-end, as defined in GitLab&#39;s IM/EM engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for customers internally and coordinate Engineering, Support, Product, Customer Success, and Sales toward resolution, tracking commitments and holding owning teams accountable to agreed dates and deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a written, customer-facing resolution plan from engagement through confirmed resolution, updating it at each communication milestone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Incident Managers during concurrent technical incidents to maintain a single, coherent narrative for the customer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own external escalation communications using GitLab&#39;s approved templates and cadence, and represent GitLab in high-stakes customer conversations where clarity and ownership influence retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage Sales, Customer Success, and executive stakeholders as needed, including executive-to-executive communication for Severity 1 and 2 events. Brief GitLab leadership with concise summaries that distinguish what&#39;s known, what&#39;s unknown, and next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead post-escalation reviews and relationship repair plans, contribute corrective actions with named owners and due dates to postmortems, and hand the relationship back to the account&#39;s Customer Success Manager at resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of IM/EM to develop playbooks, communication templates, and process improvements based on patterns from escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in enterprise technical support, customer success, or incident and escalation management at a business-to-business software-as-a-service or enterprise software company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of owning complex, multi-stakeholder escalations end-to-end, including executive customer engagements and structured resolution or account plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive-level written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to translate technical detail into plain-language updates for customers and GitLab leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to coordinate Engineering, Support, Product, Customer Success, and Sales under pressure without formal authority over those teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm, structured decision-making with incomplete information and the ability to provide a steadying presence in high-stress customer situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with support and coordination tools such as Zendesk, Salesforce, Slack, and PagerDuty, or equivalent platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability for on-call coverage supporting executive escalations as part of a globally distributed team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&amp;nbsp; &lt;/strong&gt;Information Technology Infrastructure Library (ITIL) Foundation or equivalent certification; customer-facing experience with GitLab, development, security, and operations (DevSecOps), continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD), or cloud-native products; experience with formal escalation or incident command frameworks; or AI-assisted support tools for triage, sentiment analysis, or resolution drafting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Incident &amp;amp; Escalation Management function sits within Support Engineering in GitLab&#39;s Enterprise Technology &amp;amp; AI (ETA) division. We operate a follow-the-sun model anchored in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East and Africa, and Asia-Pacific, providing year-round, 24-hour coverage for enterprise customers. Our Escalation Managers work globally rather than within a single region, partnering with Incident Managers, Communications Leads, and regional Support Engineering leadership. You&#39;ll help shape our playbooks, templates, and standards as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
