&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;Intermediate Fullstack Engineer, Subscription Lifecycle (Monetization)&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Remote, AMEA&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Intermediate Fullstack Engineer on GitLab&#39;s Subscription Lifecycle team within Monetization, you&#39;ll build the frontend experiences and backend services customers use to view and manage subscriptions, renew products, configure auto-renewal, and manage billing accounts. Your work will span renewals, overages and reconciliations, subscription visibility, and budget and reservation management, keeping subscription, billing, and account data accurate and reliable. Because these workflows directly affect revenue, customer access, and financial information, you&#39;ll use technical judgment, safe and iterative rollouts, and a high bar for reliability and correctness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Some examples of our projects:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Building a clear, reliable subscription view across the Customers Portal and related surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Improving manual renewal and auto-renewal flows, including supporting emails, banners, and account experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Design and build fullstack features across the post-purchase subscription journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Contribute to the technical design and implementation of new subscription lifecycle capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Partner with Product and Design to translate renewal, billing account, and customer experience requirements into resilient, well-tested solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Integrate subscription lifecycle workflows safely with billing, customer account, and internal admin systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;Write maintainable, well-tested code and follow engineering practices for rollout safety and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;Participate in code reviews and provide thoughtful, constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Identify and reduce technical debt and architectural risk in the subscription lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Participate in incident response for subscription and renewal issues, given their potential impact on revenue and customer access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Professional experience as a fullstack engineer and confidence working across frontend and backend code. Our purchase applications use Ruby on Rails and Vue.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;Experience owning technical direction for a product area, including proposing, discussing, and driving thorough, iterative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;Experience building or maintaining transactional or checkout-style flows, ideally in a billing, ecommerce, or subscription context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;Familiarity integrating with third-party billing or customer relationship management systems, such as Zuora, Salesforce, or Stripe, is a plus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;A focus on safe, incremental delivery given the revenue and customer impact of this work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;The ability to communicate clearly and concisely about complex technical, architectural, and organizational problems and propose thorough, iterative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;Written and spoken English proficiency sufficient to collaborate in a remote, largely asynchronous work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;Alignment with GitLab&#39;s values and a commitment to working in accordance with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Subscription Lifecycle team is part of GitLab&#39;s Monetization section and owns the post-purchase subscription experience. You&#39;ll partner with Sales, Finance, Information Technology, and Support on secure, reliable purchasing, billing, provisioning, and utilization workflows, and report to the Engineering Manager, Purchase. The team works asynchronously, with regular planning and retrospectives and shared expectations for deployments, incident management, testing, and rollout safety. GitLab&#39;s mission is to enable everyone to contribute and co-create the software that powers our world. The Purchase team&#39;s mission is to make it as easy as possible for anyone to buy, add on to, or upgrade GitLab through a single, trustworthy, unified purchase experience. For more on how Monetization works, see the &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/engineering/development/monetization/&quot;&gt;Monetization sub-department handbook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;2&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/all-remote/asynchronous/&quot;&gt;All remote, asynchronous work environment&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;3&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/paid-time-off/&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;4&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/erg-guide/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;5&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/#employee-stock-purchase-plan-espp&quot;&gt;Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;6&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#growth-and-development-benefit&quot;&gt;Growth and development budget&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;7&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental leave&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li value=&quot;8&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/finance/procurement/office-equipment-supplies/&quot;&gt;Home office support&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$115,200&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$194,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Présentation du poste :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous recherchons un(e) Senior Data Consultant(e) pour accompagner la transformation Data &amp;amp; IA de nos clients C-Level (COMEX, marketing, digital, supply-chain, opérations, customer support, IT...). Le/la consultant(e) pilote avec une large autonomie des projets complets de bout en bout, supervisé(e) par un n+1 (manager, directeur, partner), et encadre les consultants plus juniors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missions :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter un ou plusieurs streams : garantir le delivery, identifier les points de blocage, proposer des solutions, assurer la gestion de projet (documentation, planning, comptes-rendus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encadrer et donner des feedbacks constructifs aux membres juniors de l&#39;équipe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produire de manière autonome les livrables de mission : présentations, benchmarks, études de cas, workshop decks, sections steerco&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rédiger des storylines et concevoir des slides percutantes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Animer les interviews et workshops clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Construire une relation de confiance avec les clients et identifier des opportunités business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer au développement d&#39;Artefact : développement d&#39;une offre, d&#39;une industrie, d&#39;un chapter ou d&#39;un partenariat école ; participation au recrutement et à la formation des nouveaux arrivants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Soutenir et développer une ou plusieurs expertises internes (stratégie, data governance, data marketing...) via la construction d&#39;offres, la formation, ou des actions marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profil recherché :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 à 3 ans d&#39;expérience professionnelle en cabinet de conseil&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Double profil &quot;business&quot; et &quot;data&quot; : curieux(se), passionné(e) par la data et les évolutions technologiques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Esprit analytique, goût pour la résolution de problèmes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expérience en gestion de clients et identification d&#39;opportunités commerciales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise de la Suite Google/Pack Office et des outils de workshop ; excellente communication en français et en anglais (écrit/oral)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Localisation en plein cœur de Paris (9ème arrondissement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Environnement pluridisciplinaire en forte croissance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formations régulières et montée en compétences sur les méthodes de travail tech (product mindset, agilité)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture entrepreneuriale fondée sur l&#39;innovation, la collaboration et l&#39;action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process de recrutement :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Interview&lt;/strong&gt; : 30/45&#39; - entretien de motivation, culture et éligibilité avec un(e) Talent Acquisition Specialist&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consulting Manager &lt;/strong&gt;: Business case - partie fit (motivation, soft skills, valeurs) puis use case avec synthèse de la solution (réponse, durée, équipe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Consulting Director&lt;/strong&gt; : Business case - partie fit (motivation, soft skills, valeurs) puis use case avec synthèse de la solution (réponse, durée, équipe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner&lt;/strong&gt; : Business case - partie fit (motivation, soft skills, valeurs) puis use case avec synthèse de la solution (réponse, durée, équipe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération &lt;/strong&gt;: 53 000€ à 63 000€ brut annuel (fixe) + jusqu’à 5 000€ de variable selon expérience et séniorité&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Présentation entreprise :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact est un cabinet de conseil spécialisé en data et en intelligence artificielle, qui accompagne les entreprises pour transformer ces technologies en impact business concret et mesurable.&amp;nbsp;A la croisée du conseil, de la data et de la technologie, nos 2 500 collaborateurs dans 27 pays mettent leurs expertises en commun pour concevoir, développer et déployer des solutions qui répondent aux enjeux de transformation de nos clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Envie d&#39;en savoir plus? Découvrez Artefact, nos expertises et notre culture : https://www.artefact.com&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion et diversité :&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Artefact, nous sommes convaincus que la diversité des parcours, des expériences et des perspectives fait la richesse de nos équipes. Nous nous engageons à offrir un environnement inclusif et des opportunités équitables, où chacune et chacun peut évoluer et exprimer pleinement son potentiel. Nos recrutements reposent sur les compétences, le potentiel et l&#39;adéquation avec le rôle.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Charles River Associates&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com&quot;&gt;Charles River Associates&lt;/a&gt; is a leading global consulting firm that provides economic, financial, and business management expertise to major law firms, corporations and governments around the world. CRA advises clients on economic and financial matters pertaining to litigation and regulatory proceedings, and guides corporations through critical business strategy and performance-related issues. Since 1965, clients have engaged CRA for its combination of industry experience and rigorous, fact-based analyses that provide clients with clear, implementable solutions to complex business concerns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA&#39;s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/services/antitrust-and-competition/ecp/&quot;&gt;European Competition practice&lt;/a&gt; specialises in providing economic advice on matters of competition policy and regulation. We assist firms and their legal advisors in all types of competition proceedings: &amp;nbsp;firms considering merger and acquisition opportunities or involved in merger control proceedings; and firms undergoing investigations relating to cartels, restrictive commercial agreements, abuse of dominance or state aid. &amp;nbsp;We also provide advice to firms involved in regulatory proceedings and sector inquiries. We offer assistance on the estimation effects of damages in cartel cases, international arbitration and intellectual property disputes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Associate position is the entry-level position for applicants with a PhD in Economics and limited work experience. The Senior Associate position is also open to applicants with a Master of Economics and at least 3 years of relevant work experience, within economic consulting or with a competition authority. Candidates will be expected to rapidly take on genuine responsibility, working closely with senior consultants, scholars and industry experts on project teams, and will have the opportunity to immediately work on some of the largest, high-profile and most significant competition cases in Europe, providing conceptual and practical input to projects. A Senior Associate would typically:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Conduct analyses and collect evidence from data and research that support our expert opinions and business recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Perform regression analyses in statistical analysis programs (such as Stata, Python, R), including large data projects requiring the use of cloud computing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build economic models tailored to the issues at hand and supporting our expert opinions and business recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Contribute to the development and presentation of client deliverables, including expert reports and white papers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Interact with clients and communicate complicated economic concepts and arguments to non-experts in an understandable, accessible manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Manage and mentor junior staff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the integrity and accuracy of analyses and opinions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in practice-building activities (training, recruiting, publication, expertise sharing, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD in economics from a well-regarded institution with a strong foundation in microeconomics, preferably with a specialisation in industrial economics and/or econometrics; non-PhD applicants should have a Master of Economics and at least 3 years of relevant work experience, within economic consulting or with a competition authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English, other language skills are considered an asset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High degree of numeracy, ability to analyse data, familiarity with econometric techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and oral communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong teamwork and collaboration capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent time management and task prioritisation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and demonstrated interest in economic consulting through coursework, work experience, or activities&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;To Apply&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis. To be considered for this position, submit through this job posting:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curriculum Vitae&lt;/strong&gt; – please include current address, email and telephone number;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Covering letter&lt;/strong&gt; – please describe your interest in a role with CRA&#39;s Antitrust and Competition Economics practice in Germany and how this role matches your goals;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Writing Sample (optional)&lt;/strong&gt; – we prefer a sole-authored submission from an existing work (work product, published article or job market paper) that includes your commentary on a quantitative analysis and/or relevant to the field of economics;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transcripts (optional) &lt;/strong&gt;- from the most recent academic training (may be unofficial copies).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CRA creates a work environment that enables our colleagues to benefit from being together in the office to best deliver on our promise of career growth, mentorship and inclusivity. At the same time, we recognise that individuals realise a range of benefits when working from home periodically. We currently expect that individuals spend at least 3 to 4 days a week working in the office (which may include traveling to another CRA office or to client meetings), with specific days determined in coordination with your practice or team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsible AI Use in Recruiting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe that recruiting is fundamentally a human process, and we are committed to a hiring process that is consistent, transparent, and people-focused. While AI and other technology-enabled tools help our team operate more efficiently, we strive to provide every candidate with a personalized, thoughtful, and high-touch experience. As CRA invests significant human effort to find qualified members for our teams, we expect candidates to invest corresponding human effort to learn about CRA, prepare thoughtful application materials, and engage with our interviewers. Read more about appropriate hiring manager, recruiting team, and candidate AI at CRA &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.crai.com/cra-careers/ai-recruiting/&quot;&gt;on our website&lt;/a&gt;. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Our Commitment to Diversity&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Charles River Associates is an equal opportunity employer. As part of our focus on equity and inclusion, we work to ensure a fair and consistent hiring process. We celebrate diversity and we are committed to an inclusive work environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The statements included in this job description are intended to describe the general nature and level of work being performed by people assigned to this job. They are not intended to be an exhaustive list of all responsibilities, duties and skills required of personnel so classified.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you&#39;re brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you&#39;re excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an Mid-Market Account Executive to join our team of high performing Account Executives in the DACH region. Figma is growing and moving fast. Our next team member will have an agile, dynamic mindset, be comfortable embracing change and a true team-player. You won’t be alone! Figma has an incredible team and you’ll work closely with other groups including Support, Design, Engineering, Product Marketing, Customer Success, and Community. You will report directly to our Commercial Sales Manager who is also based in Berlin, Germany.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full time role in our Berlin office within a hybrid environment or remote.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you’ll do at Figma:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong sales pipeline while exceeding quarterly and annual sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross functional teams to ensure sales effectiveness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain relationships with key stakeholders within Enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be part of a team dedicated to promoting Figma to existing and new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the foundation and processes for all customer facing teams at Figma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;kgm684&quot; data-start=&quot;74&quot; data-end=&quot;148&quot;&gt;Work with a dedicated set of customers, each with up to 5,000 employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We&#39;d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of closing experience working with customers, ideally with a SaaS product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about working in a fast-paced environment and helping improve business processes as we grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to learn a technical product and effectively communicate Figma’s value to potential customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambitious self-starter who’s eager to learn while being a core part of building our business from the ground up&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High attention to detail with excellent written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;While it’s not required, it’s an added plus if you also have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with UX/UI design principles and collaboration tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience using a sales methodology, ideally Command of the Message or MEDDICC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Figma we celebrate and support our differences. We know employing a team rich in diverse thoughts, experiences, and opinions allows our employees, our product and our community to flourish. Figma is an &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/EEOC_KnowYourRights_screen_reader_10_20.pdf&quot;&gt;equal opportunity workplace&lt;/a&gt; - we are dedicated to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity/expression, veteran status&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;or any other characteristic protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to &lt;a ---------- These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples of accommodations include but are not limited to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding interviews in an accessible location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling closed captioning on video conferencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring all written communication be compatible with screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changing the mode or format of interviews&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure the integrity of our hiring process and facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates keep their cameras on during video interviews. Additionally, if hired you will be required to attend in person onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with &lt;a class=&quot;c-link c-link--underline&quot; href=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-stringify-link=&quot;https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/&quot; data-sk=&quot;tooltip_parent&quot;&gt;Figma&#39;s Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application limits:&lt;/strong&gt; To help candidates focus on the opportunities most relevant to their skills and experience, Figma limits the number and frequency of applications. These limits apply to all roles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates may submit up to 5 applications during any rolling 30-day period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Candidates may not reapply to the same role while an application is active or within 90 days of receiving a rejection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Once the applicable days has passed, candidates are welcome to apply again.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior CX Platform Engineer, you&#39;ll help GitLab&#39;s Customer Experience (CX) teams hand real work to artificial intelligence (AI). You&#39;ll use Claude Code and GitLab Duo Agent Platform as your default development tools, designing agentic workflows and Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers with production testing, security, and shared ownership. This is a software engineering role, not ticket-taking internal IT, AI evangelism disconnected from shipped code, or customer-billable Professional Services delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Claude Code, GitLab Duo, and other coding agents as your primary development environment for planning, implementation, refactoring, testing, reviews, and documentation. Run multiple agents in parallel on well-scoped tasks, critically review their output, and own every line that reaches production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain the team&#39;s agent harness, including shared AGENTS.md conventions, skills, slash commands, hooks, subagent definitions, and continuous integration checks. Measure and share what works, publish reusable patterns, and retire those that don&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship agents and multi-step workflows for account research, success planning, scoping, status reporting, and customer onboarding. Package them as skills and plugins for non-engineers using Claude, Claude in Slack, and GitLab Duo Agent Platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build MCP servers and connectors for governed access to GitLab, Salesforce, Gainsight, Kantata, Thought Industries, Gong, Snowflake, and other enterprise systems. Add evaluations, tracing, and human-in-the-loop checkpoints to keep internal and customer-facing agents measurable, auditable, and safe with customer data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve the CX Application Platform&#39;s gateway, Amazon Web Services (AWS) infrastructure, including Elastic Container Service (ECS), Relational Database Service (RDS), and Lambda, Terraform configuration, application scaffold, and deployment path. Own applications such as PS Compass, Congregate, and GitLab University and its integrations, documenting build-versus-buy and consolidate-or-sunset decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship production-quality Python and TypeScript through GitLab continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD), with tests, observability, security review, and runbooks. Design every application for handoff, with documentation, monitoring, and shared ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype with Customer Success, Digital Success, Professional Services, Education Services, and Training in days, not quarters. Help CX team members bring their own applications to production, and turn field learning into reusable reference implementations, development paths, and enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute upstream to GitLab and share product feedback with Product and Engineering. Mentor engineers and non-engineers on agentic development and raise the team&#39;s code review bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating production software, owning multi-quarter work from ambiguity to production, choosing reusable platform solutions over one-off customization where appropriate, and designing for handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily, hands-on use of coding agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, GitLab Duo, or similar on production work. You can show how they&#39;ve changed what you ship and how you maintain quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building with large language models (LLMs) beyond chat, including tool use, MCP servers, agent loops, context and retrieval design, prompt and workflow design, and evaluations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Python skills with FastAPI or Flask and TypeScript skills with Vue or React, including application programming interface (API) design, authentication, authorization, and secure handling of customer and business data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with AWS ECS, RDS, and Lambda, Terraform, Docker, and applications running behind single sign-on (SSO), such as Okta.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating enterprise systems through Representational State Transfer (REST) and GraphQL APIs, and fluency with Git, merge requests, and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating non-engineering stakeholders&#39; workflows into technical plans and writing clear asynchronous design documents, decision records, and enablement materials. You align with GitLab&#39;s values and are willing to use GitLab for your own work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optional experience includes agent harness customization; the GitLab Development Kit, Duo Agent Platform custom agents and flows, or AI Catalog publishing; enterprise agent governance and data controls; customer success, professional services, or learning platforms such as Salesforce, Gainsight, Kantata, or Thought Industries; professional services economics and customer success metrics; Snowflake or similar warehouses; and technical writing, talks, or open source contributions on agentic development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; you don&#39;t need to meet every nice-to-have to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;CX Platform Engineering builds and runs CX Applications for Customer Success, Digital Success, Professional Services, Education Services, and Training. We own the CX Application Platform&#39;s gateway and infrastructure alongside our application portfolio: GitLab University, the Foundational Onboarding Agent in GitLab Duo Agent Platform, Congregate, PS Compass, and Customer Wins. We build the first version with the people doing the work, turn what we learn into a reusable pattern, then hand it off so it runs without us. We reward leverage, not heroics, and don&#39;t leave tools dependent on one person.&lt;/p&gt;
